{"id": "section-body-23872", "title": "Sexual Dysfunction", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-one", "blocks": [{"id": "body-23872", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Sexual Dysfunction", "runs": [{"text": "Sexual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Dysfunction"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "535"}}, {"id": "body-23874", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Female Sexual Dysfunction", "runs": [{"text": "Female"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Sexual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Dysfunction"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "535"}}, {"id": "body-23875", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Sexual dysfunction in women refers to sexual problems associated with personal distress and may take different forms including lack of sexual drive, impaired arousal, failure to achieve orgasm or dyspareunia. Diagnostic criteria are reached when a sexual problem is recurrent/ persistent and result in personal distress.", "runs": [{"text": "Sexual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dysfunction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "women"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "refers"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sexual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "problems"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "personal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "distress"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "take"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "different"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "forms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "including lack"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sexual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "drive,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "impaired"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "arousal,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "failure"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "achieve"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "orgasm"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dyspareunia."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Diagnostic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "criteria"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reached"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "when"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sexual problem is recurrent/ persistent and result in personal distress."}]}, {"id": "body-23876", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The causes of sexual dysfunction are multifactorial and may include psychological problem (depression or anxiety), relationship conflicts, fatigue, stress, prior physical or sexual abuse, medications or physical problems that make sexual activity uncomfortable (endometriosis, genitourinary symptoms of menopause).", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "causes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sexual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dysfunction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "multifactorial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "psychological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "problem"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(depression"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "anxiety),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "relationship conflicts, fatigue, stress, prior physical or sexual abuse, medications or physical problems that make sexual activity uncomfortable (endometriosis, genitourinary symptoms of menopause)."}]}, {"id": "body-23878", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-23879", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Correction of contributing factor (genital lesion, systemic or hormonal factors and drugs e.g. SSRIs) Psychological therapies Use of antidepressants", "runs": [{"text": "Correction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "contributing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "factor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(genital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lesion,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "systemic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hormonal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "factors"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "drugs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "e.g."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "SSRIs)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Psychological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapies Use of antidepressants"}]}, {"id": "body-23880", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Male sexual dysfunction", "runs": [{"text": "Male"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sexual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dysfunction"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "535"}}, {"id": "body-23881", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It is inability to attain and maintain an erect penis with sufficient rigidity for vaginal penetration and ability to ejaculate. Organic causes include neurogenic, vasculogenic, endocrinological as well as many systemic diseases and medications.", "runs": [{"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inability"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "attain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maintain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "erect"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "penis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sufficient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rigidity"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vaginal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "penetration"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ability"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ejaculate."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Organic causes include neurogenic, vasculogenic, endocrinological as well as many systemic diseases and medications."}]}, {"id": "body-23883", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non"},